  "body": "### Summary\n\nAs a reader scrolling a list or a topic, I want the top bar's title to get out of the way when I scroll down, leaving only its buttons floating, and to come back when I scroll up, so that the content gets the whole screen as in most iOS apps. (Operator feedback, 2026-11-13, device screenshot of Favoris › Drapeaux. It applies to every scrolling screen of the app, not only Drapeaux.)\n\n### Observed\n\nThe title area (\"Drapeaux\", with refresh and \"⋯\" to its right) stays fixed at the top while the list scrolls, and takes space from the content.\n\n### Expected\n\n- **Scrolling down:** the title area goes away and the content takes its place. Only the buttons stay, floating (Liquid Glass).\n- **Scrolling up:** the title comes back.\n- Same behaviour on every screen that scrolls content: categories, topic lists, Favoris, Drapeaux, MPs, search, settings lists. The reader is to check separately, against #820 and #641 (group R).\n\n### Platform reference (sources; HIG page wording not yet read)\n\n- WWDC25 \"Build a UIKit app with the new design\" (https://developer.apple.com/videos/play/wwdc2025/284/): under the iOS 26 design, large titles sit at the top of the content scroll view and scroll with the content under the bar, while the bar's buttons stay.\n- WWDC25 \"Get to know the new design system\" (https://developer.apple.com/videos/play/wwdc2025/356/): Liquid Glass with scroll edge effects instead of hard dividers.\n- The tab bar side exists already: `tabBarMinimizeBehavior(.onScrollDown)` behind the legacy setting `tabbar_minimize_on_scroll` (`App/SwiftHFR/Root/RootTabsView.swift:39`). The top bar has no equivalent.\n- UIKit's `hidesBarsOnSwipe` (https://developer.apple.com/documentation/uikit/uinavigationcontroller/barhideonswipegesturerecognizer) hides the whole bar, buttons included. It is not what is asked.\n- **To do before coding:** read the HIG pages \"Navigation bars\" and \"Toolbars\" and cite their wording in the PR.\n\n### Likely cause, to verify\n\nAbout 26 screens force `.navigationBarTitleDisplayMode(.inline)` / `.toolbarTitleDisplayMode(.inline…)`, which pins a small title in the bar. The standard large title, `.automatic` or `.large`, scrolls away with the content and leaves the buttons. Check the legacy look at `87fe0d1c` and the M4 Liquid Glass work (#545, LOT-185/186) before changing it, so that parity and the reader chrome are not broken.\n\n### Scope\n\n- One shared choice for all list screens, not a per-screen tweak (#836).\n- Do not change the reader in this issue: its bars are group R (#594, #820, #821, #641).\n\n### Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] On every list screen, scrolling down hides the title and keeps the buttons; scrolling up brings the title back.\n- [ ] iPhone and iPad (split view), light and dark, Dynamic Type XL checked on the Mac.\n- [ ] The HIG wording is cited in the PR.\n\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_",
